ferrometer (0.5.0-3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Fix: 0.5.0-2 installed the unit where bookworm's debhelper does not
    look, so the package carried no maintainer scripts and the service was
    neither enabled, started nor restarted on upgrade. The unit now goes
    through debian/ferrometer.service.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 14:50:18 +0200

ferrometer (0.5.0-2) stable; urgency=medium

  * Rebuild as a dh-based source package from the release tag, replacing
    the hand-rolled .deb attached to the GitHub release. Service handling
    (enable, start, restart on upgrade) now comes from dh_installsystemd.
  * Build with the rustup stable toolchain: the locked crates need rustc
    1.86 or newer, well past what bookworm packages.

 -- Roman Kivalin <roman@shl.dev>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:06:11 +0200
